### The problem

Dust-generating activities can include:

* Construction sites without adequate dust-control practices.

* Uncovered sand, soil and construction materials.

* Dust from road excavation and repair.

* Construction waste left near roads.

* Roads that remain dusty after construction activity.

The problem is not simply that dust exists. It is that citizens and inspectors need a practical way to document its sources, identify repeated problems and follow up on corrective action.

### Proposed solution

| Problem                                           | DustShield feature    | Result                    |
| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------- |
| Citizens cannot easily document a problem         | DustMap reporting     | Location-based reports    |
| Construction dust controls are difficult to track | DustGuard checklist   | Recorded site assessments |
| Repeated dust problems are hard to prioritise     | Priority Intelligence | Ranked hotspots           |
| Cleaning and inspections need coordination        | CleanRoad             | Action tracking           |
| Nobody can see whether action was taken           | Before/after evidence | Visible progress          |

### What makes it different?

A normal complaint application collects reports.

DustShield connects the complete process:

1\. Report

Citizen or inspector submits a dust observation

2\. Assess

Construction dust-control checklist

3\. Prioritise

Rank repeated and unresolved hotspots

4\. Take action

Inspection, road cleaning or corrective action

5\. Verify

Upload evidence and update report status

